.TH GPAPERD.TOML 5 2026-11-27 "gpaperd 0.1.1" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
gpaperd.toml \- gpaperd configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gpaperd/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR gpaperd (1)
reads one TOML file, by default
.I ~/.config/gpaperd/config.toml
(override with
.BR \-\-config ).
The tables
.BR [general] ,
.B [light]
and
.B [dark]
are all optional, and so is every key.
An unknown table or key is an error.
Every error names the line and column of the offending key or value.
.PP
The daemon applies an edit while it runs, including an edit through a
symlink into a dotfiles repository; relative paths resolve against the
directory of the real file, every symlink followed.
An invalid edit is logged and the running config stays.
A missing file at start is not an error: the daemon idles until it appears.
An invalid file at start ends the daemon with exit status 78.
.PP
Check a file without a running daemon with
.BR "gpaperd check\-config" .
A commented example ships as
.IR dist/config.example.toml .
.SH [general]
.TP
.BR interval " = \(dq15m\(dq"
Time between two changes of the style on screen, as a duration such as
.BR 90s ,
.B 15m
or
.BR 1h ,
from 1 minute to 1 hour inclusive.
.TP
.BR order " = \(dqrandom\(dq"
.B random
is a shuffle bag: every image once per round, in a fresh order, and a new
round never starts with the image on screen.
.B alphabetical
is a natural, case-insensitive sort on the file name (a URL's last path
segment); after a deleted image it goes on with the next name.
.TP
.BR picture_options " = unset"
One of
.BR wallpaper ,
.BR centered ,
.BR scaled ,
.BR stretched ,
.B zoom
or
.BR spanned ,
written to GNOME's
.B picture\-options
key.
Unset leaves the key alone, except that
.B none
(which shows no image) is turned into
.BR zoom .
.B none
is refused here.
.TP
.BR on_external_change " = \(dqpause\(dq"
What happens when something else changes a style's background key, for
example a wallpaper picked in Settings.
.B pause
stops that style until
.BR "gpaperctl resume" ,
a config reload, or the key points at
.B gpaperd
again.
.B reassert\-next\-tick
writes the key back at the next change.
.B reassert\-now
writes it back after 1 second; more than 3 changes within a minute mean
another tool is fighting over the key, and the style pauses.
.TP
.BR rotate_hidden " = false"
Rotate the style that is not on screen too.
When false its slot keeps the last image it showed, and its interval counts
only the time it is on screen.
.TP
.BR empty_style " = \(dquse\-other\-style\(dq"
What a style without any usable image shows.
.B use\-other\-style
gives it the other style's current image;
.B keep\-current
leaves its slot as it is.
.TP
.BR remote_refresh " = \(dqstartup\(dq"
When cached remote images are checked for a new version.
.B startup
once per daemon start;
a duration of at least 1 hour, such as
.BR 24h ,
at start and then that often;
.B never
downloads only what is not cached.
.TP
.BR link " = true"
Fill a slot by hardlink, else reflink, else copy.
.B false
always copies, so editing an original in place never changes the desktop.
.TP
.BR apply_mode " = \(dqslots\(dq"
.B slots
points the background keys at two slot files once and rotates by replacing
the files.
.B uri
writes each image's own
.B file://
URI to the keys instead: the fallback for a GNOME release that does not
reload a replaced slot file.
.TP
.BR max_pixels " = 100_000_000"
Skip images whose width times height is larger.
A whole number greater than zero.
.TP
.BR pause_when_locked " = false"
Stop the timers of both styles while the screen is locked, as
.B org.gnome.ScreenSaver
reports it on the session bus.
A change that fell due meanwhile happens at unlock.
A session without that service is no error: the daemon logs it once and
keeps listening.
.SH [light] AND [dark]
.TP
.B interval
.TQ
.B order
Override the
.B [general]
value for this style.
.TP
.BR sources " = []"
A list of sources, in any mix.
A style with no sources is valid; see
.BR empty_style .
.SH SOURCES
A plain string is classified by its prefix:
.TP
.B http://\fR...\fP, https://\fR...\fP
A remote image, downloaded into
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gpaperd/remote .
A cached copy is shown at once, even offline, and revalidated in the
background.
A URL whose host is a loopback, unspecified
.RB ( 0.0.0.0 ", " [::] ),
private or link-local IP address is not fetched and not retried; use a
host name.
A redirect to such an address, or from https to http, is not followed.
A URL refused that way, or answered with 401, 403, a non-image or an
oversized body, keeps its cached copy; with nothing cached it counts as
gone for
.BR empty_style .
.TP
.B file://\fR...\fP
A percent-decoded absolute path on this machine.
.TP
.I anything else
A path. Whether it is a directory or a file is decided when it is scanned,
so a path that does not exist yet is not an error; its images join when it
appears.
.PP
Any other
.B scheme://
is an error. A table gives options:
.TP
.B { dir = \(dq\fIpath\fP\(dq }
A directory, with the optional keys
.B recursive
(false; descend up to 16 levels),
.B hidden
(false; include names starting with a dot),
.B follow_symlinks
(true) and
.B poll
(unset; a period of at least 1 second, for a file system where inotify does
not see changes).
NFS, CIFS, SMB2 and FUSE file systems are polled every 5 minutes without it.
.TP
.B { file = \(dq\fIpath\fP\(dq }
One file, taken whatever its name.
.TP
.B { url = \(dq\fIurl\fP\(dq }
A remote image.
.PP
In a directory, files count by extension:
.BR jpg ,
.BR jpeg ,
.BR png ,
.BR webp ,
.BR jxl ,
.BR avif ,
.BR heic ,
.BR heif ,
.BR tif ,
.BR tiff ,
.BR bmp ,
.B gif
and
.BR qoi ,
in any case.
Each image is still checked before use, by its magic bytes and a decode in
glycin's sandbox.
A file reached through two sources, a symlink or a hardlink counts once.
A file whose name is not valid UTF-8 is skipped with the scan warning
.IR "file name is not UTF-8" .
.SH PATHS
A leading
.B \(ti
becomes
.BR $HOME .
.B $VAR
and
.B ${VAR}
are expanded from the environment, and an undefined variable is an error.
A relative path resolves against the directory of the real config file.
A
.B $
that starts no name stands for itself.
Write a path that holds a literal
.B $NAME
as a
.B file://
URI.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
[general]
interval = "15m"
order = "random"
pause_when_locked = true

[light]
sources = [
  "\(ti/Pictures/Wallpapers/light",
  { dir = "\(ti/Pictures/Wallpapers/shared", recursive = true },
  "https://example.com/wallpapers/dawn.jpg",
]

[dark]
interval = "30m"
order = "alphabetical"
sources = [
  { dir = "/mnt/nas/wallpapers/dark", poll = "5m" },
  "file:///srv/wall/aurora%20night.png",
]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpaperd (1),
.BR gpaperctl (1)
